        },
        "text": "=You write an Instagram caption for \"Sailing Nomads\", a personal sailing and travel blog by a Swiss couple sailing Europe with their dog Charly. Goal: reach, saves and profile visits; the blog link lives in the bio. Write in English. This is one short reel from the blog post titled \"{{ $(\"Parse Reel Payload\").item.json.post.title }}\". Base the caption ONLY on this section. Section title: {{ $(\"Parse Reel Payload\").item.json.video.section_title }}. Section text: \n\n{{ $(\"Parse Reel Payload\").item.json.video.section_text }}. \n\nThe section text contains a [VIDEO] marker showing where this reel's clip sits in the surrounding prose; the sentence describing the clip may come just before or just after the marker, so rely on the text nearest the marker and treat the rest as background. The attached image is the reel cover frame; use it for concrete visual detail. The first line must hook within about 125 characters. Short airy paragraphs, emojis welcome but not overloaded. End with a question or a save-this nudge. Avoid AI tells: never use the em dash; avoid words like delve, tapestry, vibrant, crucial, seamless, robust, leverage, foster, realm, and journey cliches. Sound like a real person writing to friends. Do NOT include any URL or a link-in-bio call to action. Do not invent facts not in the section. After the caption, add 5 to 8 specific hashtags on their own final line, each starting with #, mixing niche sailing and travel tags with location tags, avoiding banned or spammy tags. Return ONLY the caption text followed by that hashtag line.",
        "inputType": "base64",
        "options": {
          "detail": "auto",
          "maxTokens": 500
        }
      },
